                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.731/135: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-10-10T19:00:00-05:00">October 10, 1939—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1210. Your 2397, October 10, 11 a.m. Department gratified that French authorities
                    will authorize codes mentioned in your 2203. However, before giving out this
                    information, Department desires exact date upon which new regulations will be
                    effective. Please endeavor to obtain this information and forward it to the
                    Department in order that information contained in your 2397 may be made
                    public.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
